Wt is Dockerfile
=============

	Ø Whenever you want to write any dockerfile you should have app source code
	Ø Dockerfile name should be like this only " Dockerfile"

FROM:- it is used to specify a base image for the application .

FROM ubuntu:latest - for static web application

FROM  node:latest

FROM python:3.10-alpine3.24

===========================================================================

MAINTAINER:- it is use for to define dockerfile author or owner

MAINTAINER davidprabhakr526@gmail.com  or Y david Prabhakar

======================================================

WORKDIR:- it is used to create a working directory inside the container to contain app src, lib, depn, files and folders

WORKDIR /app

WORDKRI /ayyanna

WORKDIR /david

==================================================================

COPY:- it is used to copy app source code from local machine to container machine

COPY <scr code location>  <destination location>

COPY index.html /var/www/html

COPY . .

====================================================================

ADD:- it is used to handle URL's in dockerfile 

ADD https://dlcdn.apache.org/tomcat/tomcat-9/v9.0.121/bin/apache-tomcat-9.0.121-windows-x86.zip

ADD https://www.java.com/en/download/linux_manual.jsp

=======================================================================================

	Ø Dockerfile will build image in two stages
	1. Build time  - commands should be execute while building the docker image
	2. RUN time  - commands should be execute while creating the container

RUN:- it is used to execute commands while building the docker image

RUN apt update -y

RUN yum update -y

RUN apt install apache2 -y

RUN apt install java -y

RUN apt install npm -y

RUN apt install docker -y

RUN apt install git -y

RUN yum install java -y

RUN yum install docker -y

==========================================================================

EXPOSE:- it is used to define or expose the application port number

EXPOSE 9000

EXPOSE 8000

EXPOSE 3000

=======================================================================

CMD:- it will execute commands while creating the container to start the application inside the container 

node start 

Python app.py

Python start

CMD ["node", "start"]

CMD ["node", "app.js"]

CMD ["node", "server.js"]



CMD ["python", "app.py"]

	Ø CMD will overwrite commands

=========================================================================

ENTRYPOINT:- it will execute commands while creating the container to start app inside the container but it wont overwrite commands in  dockerfile

ENTRPYPOINT ["node", "start"]

